{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BxuMjqqr2or93zUqdR7vC7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Detective control for the main-lane committer (docs/proposal.md, \"The .ard/\n# contract\"). The bot bypasses branch protection on main, so this audits the\n# first-parent history of main and fails when a commit made by the bot changes\n# anything except regular files under a single .ard/<issue#>/ directory.\n#\n# The bot login and the optional baseline come from repository variables, which\n# the GitHub App cannot write. The App also lacks the `workflows` permission,\n# so it cannot edit this file. Both are why the logic is inline bash here and\n# not Go. internal/botcheck extracts the script below and tests it.\nname: ard bot commits\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  # Main-lane bot pushes carry [skip ci], which suppresses the push trigger, so\n  # a schedule is what catches a stretch of history made only of bot commits.\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '17 * * * *'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    steps:\n\n- A directory with `prompt.txt` is an agent role; a scanner directory with an executable `scan` is a deterministic scanner.\n- A `Dockerfile` builds the role's image; without one the local executor runs a host subprocess and the Kubernetes executor uses the default `ard-agent` image (agent CLIs, git, common linters). A role that reads untrusted input without one triggers the host-mode warning (see Executors and the Reaper).\n- Any other file in the directory (scripts, allowlists) is mounted read-only beside the prompt.\n\n```yaml\nmax_pods: 3                  # job slots shared by every loop\nexecutor: local              # local | k8s\nagent: claude                # default CLI for agent roles\nrequire_approval: true       # human adds ard:approved before a worker starts\nbudget_usd_per_day: 50       # whole repo, UTC day, blocks at spent >= cap; a role may set its own; provisional, recalibrated between Gate 1 and Gate 2\nmax_budget_usd: 5            # per job; provisional, same recalibration\nglobal_max_open: 30          # open scanner issues across all scanners\npaused: false\nintervals: { scanners: 4h, triage: 15m, workers: 5m, reviewers: 5m, merger: 5m, prwatch: 5m }\npr_watch: { pending_timeout: 2h }   # at least intervals.prwatch, at most 7d\nintake: { mode: label }     # mode: all | label; label (label mode only) defaults to ard:pending, must start with ard: and must not be one of ard's own labels\nmerge:                       # defaults written by `ard init`; the list is the only source (no floor in code)\n  protected_paths: [.github/, .ard/config.yaml, .ard/scanners/, .ard/triage/, .ard/workers/, .ard/reviewers/, \"**/CODEOWNERS\", CLAUDE.md, \"**/CLAUDE.md\", AGENTS.md, \"**/AGENTS.md\", .claude/, .mcp.json, \"**/.golangci.yml\", \"**/.golangci.yaml\", \"**/.golangci.toml\", \"**/.golangci.json\"]\n01M83ZSXRK7C28932RRA96PGNEt1.home\n01M83ZSXRPM7RD1MYY81GJ3QBCt1.home\n01M842VJP6RFPSDR91KVKJ8SSGt1.home\n01M8441GT2WFDSJGQCKPBPRZCNt1.home\n01M845TZS7KR1FRJD7PGDSW6V5t1.home\n01M845TZSZ9HQ1S50AVN0VYV4Dt1.home\n01M847K69M0VANMV80J07WW9VEt1.home\n01M84E8EKE746ZDPN74WKZW8CZ\n01M84E8EKE746ZDPN74WKZW8CZ.home\n01M84FTN02QDY138JKK3XFY0TJ\n01M84FTN02QDY138JKK3XFY0TJ.home\n01M84G151GXMQAZ0PVRB5SV7WA\n01M84G151GXMQAZ0PVRB5SV7WA.home\n01M84GZR7FQGDSAKVN50H429DG\n01M84GZR7FQGDSAKVN50H429DG.home\n01M84J0P3NSXC5JG4KPRZNMJ3H\n01M84J0P3NSXC5JG4KPRZNMJ3H.home\n01M84J30CJ0E8PQNEJFC30B2JQ\n01M84J30CJ0E8PQNEJFC30B2JQ.home\n01M84J4JSS10J35BM5VA3TKA4Y\n01M84J4JSS10J35BM5VA3TKA4Y.home\n01M84J4NSACT7MTNF6FRRKWFR9\n01M84J4NSACT7MTNF6FRRKWFR9.home\n01M84MHDF09HRV5Y6GQ78P2Z90\n01M84MHDF09HRV5Y6GQ78P2Z90.home\n01M84MHDGJYYCKAQVQPD7WXVXD\n01M84MHDGJYYCKAQVQPD7WXVXD.home\n01M84MHDMRY6M76ZP47EERKQ3B\n01M84MHDMRY6M76ZP47EERKQ3B.home\n01M84MM5EGYN6XYF3NM1Q9Q5YR\n01M84MM5EGYN6XYF3NM