{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMsGKpDSbSP9PWMU59JB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":27581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ce73ad0-b6b7-42dc-b456-d663d5942b35","uuid":"1c315550-244a-4693-b79a-ea2ffe6888ce","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:55:23.817Z","request_id":"req_011ChMsGKStavEC1nNWAAijV","thinking_duration_ms":308,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMsGKpDSbSP9PWMU59JB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016ZB8DSDFaPYeKWX4jGWYzR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md <<'EOF'\n# Onboard another repository (#304)\n\nHow to run ard on a second repository, by hand and in order. The model is one\n`ard serve` per repository. See\n[docs/proposal.md: Rollout](../proposal.md#rollout) and\n[Configuration](../proposal.md#configuration).\n\nEach `ard serve` has its own GitHub credentials (a GitHub App installation, or a\nfine-grained PAT after #302), its own state directory and its own limits. ard\ndoes not coordinate across processes. Roles live in the repository's own\n`.ard/`.\n\n## 1. Install the GitHub App\n\nInstall the App on the target repository only. A fine-grained PAT is an\nalternative only once #302 lands; until then use the App.\n\n## 2. Initialise the repository\n\n```sh\nard init --repo <owner>/<name>\n```\n\nThis opens an `ard-init` PR. Merge it with **Squash** or a **merge commit**,\nnever a rebase merge (see the `ard init` lane in\n[Guardrails](../proposal.md#guardrails)).\n\n## 3. Sync labels\n\n```sh\nard labels sync\n```\n\n## 4. Branch protection on `main`\n\nProtect `main` with a ruleset and put the App on its bypass list (mode Always).\nThe committer pushes `.ard/<issue#>/` commits straight to `main`; see \"Branch\nprotection and the bot\" in the proposal.\n\n## 5. Copy the bot-commit audit\n\nBy hand, in the target repository (do not edit `.github/` here): copy\n`.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from this repository, then set the\nrepository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login.\n\n## 6. Set this serve's limits\n\n`max_pods`, `budget_usd_per_day` and `max_budget_usd` in `.ard/config.yaml` apply\nto this `ard serve` alone. When a host or cluster runs more than one, set each\nserve's limits so the **total** fits the host, the cluster and the model\nsubscription.\n\nWorked example: two repositories, A and B, share one host and one subscription.\nThe host runs 4 jobs at once and the budget for the subscription is 60 USD a day.\n\n| Setting | Repo A | Repo B | Total |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `max_pods` | 2 | 2 | 4 (the host's capacity) |\n| `budget_usd_per_day` | 30 | 30 | 60 (the daily budget) |\n| `max_budget_usd` (per job) | 5 | 5 | at most 4 jobs x 5 = 20 in flight |\n\nIf A is the busier repository, give it more of both, but keep each column's sum\nwithin the total.\n\n**Token caps.** ard has no token-cap setting today, and this runbook does not\ninvent one. Divide the subscription's token allowance through `max_pods` and the\ndollar caps above. Each serve records a usage limit on its own, so one serve\nhitting the subscription limit does not stop the other until it hits it too.\n\n## 7. Dry run, soak, go live\n\n```sh\nard serve --dry-run\n```\n\nDry-run keeps its own state in `~/.ard/state-dryrun/<owner>/<repo>/` and writes\nintended effects to `effects.jsonl`. Soak and read the ledger, then start\n`ard serve` without the flag.\n\nIn the cluster, add an entry for the repository to the instances list in the\ndeployment repository (check the key name in that repository's docs). Live agent\njobs in the cluster need #54; until it lands, run the cluster instance in\ndry-run only.\n\n## 8. Optional: a shared roles repository\n\n`roles_repo: {repo: <owner>/<name>, ref: <ref>}` in `.ard/config.yaml` loads\nroles from a shared repository, and the repository's own role of the same name\nwins. Pin a full commit SHA. The shared roles repository is tracked in #59; use\nthis only where it is available. See\n[Configuration](../proposal.md#configuration).\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"See Delivery. ard supports macOS and Linux only; Windows is unsupported.\\n\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\\n**One `ard serve` per repository.** To run ard on another repository, start a second `ard serve` for it; limits and credentials belong to each process (see Configuration). The steps are in [the onboarding runbook](runbooks/onboard-repo.md).\\n\",1)\nb=\"**Shared roles.**\"\nassert b in s\ns=s.replace(b,\"**Limits and credentials are per `ard serve`.** `max_pods`, `budget_usd_per_day` and `max_budget_usd` apply to one process. ard does not coordinate across processes, so when a host or cluster runs more than one `ard serve`, the operator sets every serve's limits together so the total fits the host, the cluster and the model subscription. Each `ard serve` has its own GitHub credentials: a GitHub App installation, or a fine-grained PAT after #302. See [the onboarding runbook](runbooks/onboard-repo.md).\\n\\n\"+b,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/layout.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"operator runbooks (gate runs, live checks)\",\"operator runbooks (gate runs, live checks, repo onboarding)\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all; git diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":27581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ce73ad0-b6b7-42dc-b456-d663d5942b35","uuid":"55faef9f-20b2-409b-9ff0-6c6a4fc97c80","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:55:34.539Z","request_id":"req_011ChMsGKStavEC1nNWAAijV"}
