{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMsHYSmAEF7VT536GRY9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the onboarding runbook and the per-serve limits and credentials note. I wrote the report to `.ard/304/worker-engineer.md`. This is a docs-only change, so I ran no Go tests or linter. I checked the relative links and the worked-example totals by reading.\n\n- **Runbook:** `docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md` is new. It covers the eight steps in order. The worked example is two repos on one host and one subscription: `max_pods` 2 and 2, `budget_usd_per_day` 30 and 30, `max_budget_usd` 5 each.\n- **Proposal:** `docs/proposal.md` gets one paragraph in Rollout (one `ard serve` per repo) and one in Configuration (limits and credentials are per process).\n- **Layout:** `docs/layout.md` now says the runbooks directory includes repo onboarding.\n\nThree things to know:\n- **Token caps:** ard has no token-cap setting, so the runbook says that and doesn't invent one. It tells the operator to divide the subscription allowance through `max_pods` and the dollar caps. You may want a separate issue for a real token cap.\n- **`instances` entry:** I couldn't find the name in this repo's docs, so the runbook words it generically and points to the deployment repo's docs.\n- **Pending features:** PAT support (#302), live cluster jobs (#54) and the shared roles repo (#59) are worded as conditional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":583,"cache_read_input_tokens":30965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":583},"output_tokens":476,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ce73ad0-b6b7-42dc-b456-d663d5942b35","uuid":"a46bcbb9-fced-449f-a61b-b2d44fa